{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LowestCommonAncestors","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For vertices at preorder positions p < q, the answer is the vertex at the least position among","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the parents of the vertices at positions p + 1 … q. Those parents lie in the answer’s subtree","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and include it, and it has the least position there. A query is therefore one range minimum","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"over n − 1 parent positions, answered by 64-entry blocks with a bitmask of each prefix’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"minimum stack and a sparse table over the blocks’ minima. Memory is about 20 bytes per vertex,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"plus (n\/64)·log₂(n\/64) entries for the table.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/TreeAlgorithms\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Lowest common ancestors of a rooted tree or arborescence, each in O(1) after O(n) work."}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Structure","modules":[{"name":"TreeAlgorithms"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"LowestCommonAn